  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Mumbai: Medical technology company BD (Becton, Dickinson and Company) has introduced its <a href=\"/tag/ultracor+twirl+breast+tissue+markers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">UltraCor Twirl breast tissue markers</a> in India.<a href=\"/tag/breast+tissue+markers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Breast tissue markers</a> are implanted during or after a biopsy to mark the location of suspicious lesions and facilitate accurate future localization for surgery, imaging follow-up, and treatment planning, particularly when lesions are no longer visible post-procedure.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>According to BD, The UltraCor Twirl Breast Tissue Markersare designed for enhanced stability and precise placement, the Twirl marker supports improved procedural confidence through reduced migration risk and visibility across ultrasound, mammography, and MRI.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>BD said the technology is essential for breast cancer patients who often undergo prolonged treatment pathways involving serial imaging, neoadjuvant therapy, surgery, and follow-up surveillance.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>It added, “In patients at risk of disease recurrence or where lesion response needs to be monitored over time, accurate marking of lesion locations is critical for tracking treatment progress, ensuring procedural accuracy, and supporting informed clinical decision-making throughout the patient journey.”</p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Oct 28, 2026 at 06:14 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Oct 28, 2026 at 06:14 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-lab